 "limitations": [
  "Bundled workloads run on the host in constrained child processes (fresh interpreter, scrubbed environment, rlimits, timeouts), not on dedicated benchmark hardware; read the warnings and the environment fingerprint before trusting small differences.",
  "Correctness validation covers only the tests and inputs it exercised. It is evidence of equivalence, not a proof.",
  "tracemalloc (Python-traced allocations during the call) and RSS (sampled process memory) measure different things and are never compared with each other.",
  "cProfile times are inflated by instrumentation: the profile shows where time goes, the benchmark shows how fast the code runs.",
  "Only 5 timed runs per variant: p95 and the bootstrap CI are unstable at this sample size; re-run with more runs on a quiet machine to confirm."
